"A `plambda` given for a parameter of a poly type (rank 2, C107), whose
 body puts its region in a list bound outside it. FX-26 takes `nil`, a
 `let`'s, at a type of its own at each use, so the list there is at a
 fresh region; KFX binds a local at one type, so its region would be the
 plambda's, which then escapes it: refused."
(define-effect kfx (maxeff (read @globals) spin))
(define run (poly ((a type)) (subr pure ((poly ((r region)) (subr (alloc r) () (escape-tag int int r)))) int))
  (plambda ((a type)) (lambda (f) 0)))
(define main (subr (read (globals run)) () int)
  (lambda ()
    (let ((xs nil))
      ((proj run int)
       (plambda ((r region))
         (lambda () (car (cons (the (escape-tag int int r) (make-escape-tag)) xs))))))))
